    "title": "Planning the Spring Glaze Workshop",
    "text": "For two mugs or small bowls each:\n\n- About 1.5 lb of clay per finished piece, plus a third more for practice and trimming.\n- That is about 4 lb per person, or 32 lb for eight people.\n- Buy two 25 lb bags. The extra covers a failed piece or a ninth student.\n\nUse one clay body for the whole class, so every piece fires at the same temperature. A mid-fire stoneware is the usual choice for an electric kiln.",
